[382.149362, "i", "python3 - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport json\nR=Path('/root/results')\nsel=json.load(open(R/'select_triplets/selection_report.json'))\nvariants=json.load(open(R/'train/model_variant_comparison.json'))\nsummary={'final_test_triplet_reconstruction_efficiency':sel['triplet_reconstruction_efficiency'],'final_test_selected_truth_triplets':sel['selected_truth_triplets'],'final_test_truth_triplets':sel['inference_truth_triplets'],'final_selection_strategy':sel['selection_strategy'],'selection_strategy_iterations':sel['validation_strategy_comparison'],'classifier_hyperparameter_iterations':variants,'decision':'Retained baseline depth-5 eta-0.07 classifier because it had the largest validation pairmax triplet recall.'}\njson.dump(summary,open(R/'optimization_summary.json','w'),indent=2)\nmd=f'''# Hadronic top triplet reconstruction optimization\n\n## Workflow\n\nAll unordered GenJet index triplets were built from the complete 10,000-event ntuple. Truth labels were matched as unordered jet-index sets. Events were split exclusively by `event_id mod 5`: 60% training, 20% validation, and 20% held-out inference. The XGBoost classifier used angular separations, pair-mass ratios, triplet/pair masses, ordered jet pT, and generator b-tag observables.\n\n## Final result\n\nFinal held-out **triplet_reconstruction_efficiency: {sel['triplet_reconstruction_efficiency']:.6f}** ({sel['selected_truth_triplets']}/{sel['inference_truth_triplets']} truth triplets recovered).\n\nThe retained configuration is the depth-5 XGBoost baseline and `pairmax` selection: exhaustively choose the highest summed-score singleton or pair of mutually jet-disjoint triplets, with at most two candidates per event and no score threshold. No threshold was used because triplet-level recall is the specified primary target. The held-out collection has {sel['selected_triplets']} selected candidates in {sel['inference_events']} events; all jet-overlap and multiplicity constraints were explicitly checked.\n\n## Optimization iterations\n\n### Event selection strategies (validation)\n\n| Configuration | Triplet reconstruction efficiency | Truth selected |\n|---|---:|---:|\n'''\nfor x in sel['validation_strategy_comparison']:\n md+=f\"| {x['configuration']} | {x['validation_triplet_reconstruction_efficiency']:.6f} | {x['selected_truth']} |\\n\"\nmd+='''\n### Classifier variants with pairmax selection (validation)\n\n| Configuration | Best iteration | Validation AUC | Triplet reconstruction efficiency |\n|---|---:|---:|---:|\n'''\nfor x in variants:\n md+=f\"| {x['name']} (depth {x['max_depth']}, eta {x['eta']}) | {x['best_iteration']} | {x['validation_auc_xgb']:.6f} | {x['validation_pairmax_efficiency']:.6f} |\\n\"\nmd+='''\nThe baseline was retained: although the shallow model had essentially tied candidate AUC, its event-level disjoint-selection recall was lower. Training detail is in `train/training_report_xgb.json`, variant data in `train/model_variant_comparison.json`, and held-out inference details in `infer/inference_report_xgb.json`.\n\n## Mass sanity check\n\n`select_triplets/plots/triplet_mass_comparison.png` compares selected held-out masses against validation truth and combinatorial candidates. The selected mass distribution has median 173.1 GeV and broad 5--95% range 131.8--412.4 GeV; no artificially narrow mass-window cut was applied. Numerical comparison and interpretation are in `sanity_checks/mass_sanity_report.json` and `sanity_checks/mass_sanity_note.md`.\n'''\nopen(R/'optimization_report.md','w').write(md)\nPY\npython3 - <<'PY'\nimport pandas as pd, json\nfrom pathlib import Path\nR=Path('/root/results')\nraw=pd.read_parquet(R/'dataset_build/triplets_raw.parquet')\ninf=pd.read_parquet(R/'infer/inference_test_xgb.parquet')\nsel=pd.read_parquet(R/'select_triplets/selected_triplets.parquet')\nev=pd.read_parquet(R/'select_triplets/event_selection.parquet')\nrep=json.load(open(R/'select_triplets/selection_report.json'))\nassert {'event_id','i','j','k','is_truth','dr_ab','dr_ac','dr_bc','mij_over_m123_ab','mij_over_m123_ac','mij_over_m123_bc'} <= set(raw)\nassert {'event_id','i','j','k','is_truth','score_xgb'} <= s"]
[382.149413, "i", "et(inf)\nassert {'event_id','selected_rank','i','j','k','score','triplet_pt','triplet_eta','triplet_phi','triplet_mass'} <= set(sel)\nassert ev.n_top_selected.max() <= 2 and sel.groupby('event_id').size().max() <= 2\nfor _,g in sel.groupby('event_id'):\n    if len(g)==2: assert not (set(g.iloc[0][['i','j','k']]) & set(g.iloc[1][['i','j','k']]))\nassert int(sel.is_truth.sum())==rep['selected_truth_triplets']\nassert int(inf.is_truth.sum())==rep['inference_truth_triplets']\nprint('FINAL VALIDATION PASS')\nprint('efficiency =',rep['triplet_reconstruction_efficiency'],f\"({rep['selected_truth_triplets']}/{rep['inference_truth_triplets']})\")\nprint('candidate/event constraints valid; all required data columns present')\nprint('sanity files:',[(p.name,p.exists()) for p in [R/'sanity_checks/mass_sanity_report.json',R/'sanity_checks/mass_sanity_note.md',R/'select_triplets/plots/triplet_mass_comparison.png']])\nPY\n"]
